    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 21-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 Fabry-Perot bandpass filter on Fused Silica substrate for 1550 nm LiDAR application. Layer sequence: Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5. Enforce strict bilateral symmetry constraint: layer_6 thickness = layer_14 thickness, layer_7 = layer_13, layer_8 = layer_12, layer_9 = layer_11, layer_10 is the center cavity layer (self-symmetric). Initialize outer mirror layers (0-5, 15-20) at quarter-wave thicknesses (Ta2O5: 184.5 nm, SiO2: 267.2 nm). Initialize cavity block layers (6-14) at 225 nm mean thickness. Optimization bounds: 50-450 nm for all layers. Perturbation amplitude: ±10 nm around initialization. Evaluate transmittance spectrum at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Score: maximize transmittance at 1550 nm (weight 1.0), minimize average transmittance in 1400-1500 nm band (weight 0.5), minimize average transmittance in 1600-1700 nm band (weight 0.5). Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
